  "id": "COMPOUND:41565 - PROTEIN:813",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 4-Coumaric acid and the Kappa-type opioid receptor, as it is implicated in multiple pathways through different targets. 4-Coumaric acid is shown to interact with 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, which in turn is targeted by both Ginkgolide A and Technetium Tc-99m sestamibi, all of which ultimately target the Kappa-type opioid receptor.  This indicates a possible chain of interactions where 4-Coumaric acid may influence the activity of the Kappa-type opioid receptor through its interaction with 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C.  The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a strong and reliable relationship, but the exact mechanism by which 4-Coumaric acid affects the Kappa-type opioid receptor remains to be elucidated.  The evidence supports a potential role for 4-Coumaric acid in modulating the activity of the Kappa-type opioid receptor, but further research is needed to fully understand the underlying mechanisms.",
